            "arguments": "{\"userQuestion\":\"Weather history in London, Ohio\"}",
            "output": "Here is some weather history for London, Ohio:\n\n1. March 1-2, 2007 – Flood\n- Roads were flooded and closed; some creeks overflowed their banks. No injuries or deaths occurred. Property damage was $3,000.\n- This resulted from a cold front that brought locally heavy rainfall to southern and western Ohio.\n\n2. March 14, 2007 – Flood\n- Multiple roads flooded across the county, causing $3,000 in property damage. There were no injuries or deaths.\n- Heavy rain ahead of a cold front affected west central and central Ohio, including the Miami Valley.\n\nThese events are examples of significant weather impacts in London, Ohio, especially regarding flooding and property damage. If you need information from another time period or additional events, please let me know!\n",
